{
    "_comment": [
        "Common names for the species this fork serves, so the database tree can",
        "be searched in English.",
        "",
        "The tree's folders are Latin binomials and its leaves are build titles,",
        "so jstree's node-text search answers nothing for 'zebrafish', 'worm',",
        "'fly' or 'mouse'. That hurts the Alliance-wide deployment most, since",
        "its users are the least likely to think in Latin.",
        "",
        "Each key is what a person types. Each value is a list of substrings",
        "matched case-insensitively against a tree node's text. Every pattern",
        "here occurs in at least one label served by this host; the",
        "database_tree_search spec asserts that, so a pattern that stops",
        "matching anything fails the suite rather than going quiet."
    ],
